--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFD: the fine offset-table generator*: Fine specifications of KIL2's `genP` stages and KIL4's uniform generator `genPU` (programs
--   unchanged).  All entries are residues `< Q`, so every element operation costs `O(b)` with the
--   *local* bound `zsz (2Q) ≤ b`; loop counts enter only linearly (`cLp N c N`, since
--   `zsz N ≤ N`).  `genPU_fsp`: cost `≤ 10^9 · (n + 1) · (vol A + 1) · (b + 2)`, where `vol A` is
--   the number of table entries (blocks).  No global size bound is needed.
